{"name":"Native Soil","hex":"#887b69","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"native soil","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The country or geographical region where one was born or which one considers to be one's true homeland.","Source, place of origin, principal location, or natural habitat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/native_soil"}],"entries":[{"title":"Soil","blocks":[{"text":"Soil, also commonly referred to as earth, is a mixture of organic matter, minerals, gases, water, and organisms that together support the life of plants and soil organisms. Some scientific definitions distinguish dirt from soil by restricting the former term specifically to displaced soil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Stagnogley.JPG/330px-Stagnogley.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soil","wikidata":"Q36133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/EAgronom_4okt2023_L-1120.jpg/500px-EAgronom_4okt2023_L-1120.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/EAgronom_4okt2023_L-1120.jpg/1280px-EAgronom_4okt2023_L-1120.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/EAgronom_4okt2023_L-1120.jpg/500px-EAgronom_4okt2023_L-1120.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Soil measuring and surveying device","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEAgronom_4okt2023_L-1120.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Estructura-suelo.jpg/500px-Estructura-suelo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Estructura-suelo.jpg/500px-Estructura-suelo.jpg?u